00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
it's been about four months since  apple's iphone 13 pro has been out in  the wild and while this is hands down my  favorite iphone update of all time for  various reasons like absolutely insane  battery life and the 120hz promotion  display there are still some issues that  apple hasn't fixed for months for  example we had a ton of complaints from  users concerning the new promotion  display tech and how it doesn't exactly  reach 120 hertz when it seems like it  should and yes in my own testing i did  notice these weird occasional stutters  every now and then but it didn't really  bother me because it didn't happen often  and to be honest i thought it was  because of the way that apple was tuning  the refresh rate to match the speed that  you're scrolling or swiping because  that's exactly what they advertised but  apparently there were some deeper issues  that were causing those stutters for  example it was extremely disappointing  to see that when the iphone 13 pro first  launched 120 hertz mode was not  available for certain animations in  third-party apps and apple even told  developers that they had to make a  special entry in their app to take full  advantage of promotion which is  obviously very annoying but now the new  ios 15.4 update has finally been  released and is jam-packed with some of  the biggest features and updates that  all together fix the iphone 13 pro and  make it a much better value for a lot of  people so what i'm gonna do in this  video is go through all of the awesome  features and changes that came with ios  15.4 and explain why they're such a big  deal like the absolutely awesome new  face id with masks feature which i'll  get into in just a minute but before  that we've got to go through the major  120 hertz pro motion fix that apple has  just added so let's get right into it  apparently there was a core animation  bug that was causing third-party apps to  have issues with full 120 hertz support  and apple has finally fixed it now all  third-party apps automatically get 120hz  animations moving forward without the  software developers having to do  anything at all to make it happen which  is awesome so this now means that we  shouldn't be experiencing those weird  stutters anymore since it'll work more  like the ipad pros which christian selig  tested and confirmed but on the other  hand with animations that aren't that  quick pro motion will still be able to  dynamically go down to 60 fps to help  save battery life compared to the ipad  pro which is basically always stuck on  120 hertz while browsing and scrolling  and only really goes down to as low as  24 hertz while watching videos or movies  so the iphone does work a little bit  differently to help save battery life  and i honestly think it's why the iphone  13 pro max has the best battery life out  of any mainstream smartphone out there  and in my personal experience 120hz  promotion has been one of my all-time  favorite features of this phone so i'm  glad that apple finally addressed those  issues now moving on to by far the most  requested feature people have had for  years apple has finally enabled face id  to work while you are wearing a mask now  this is huge because the pandemic  encouraged everyone to wear masks which  instantly made face id useless for the  past couple of years but finally the new  ios 15.4 update allows you to use face  id while wearing a mask by taking a more  detailed scan of the features around  your eyes now apple does warn that it  isn't as secure and because of that they  require you to be looking directly at  the iphone  as an extra security check but the best  part is that it can still be used for  basically anything like auto filling  your email and password for apps or  websites that use face id and it'll even  allow you to use apple pay and purchase  apps in the app store all while wearing  a mask and if you're wondering what that  pattern is on my mask yes it's little  apple product icons and we have it  available in either white or black if  you're interested in ordering one which  you can do in the merch shelf right  below this video and if you're someone  who wears glasses apple even took care  of that so it seems like people will no  longer have to complain about face id  anymore and because of this new feature  i'm starting to doubt that apple is  going to be adding in-display touch id  to the iphone in the future because in  reality if this new feature works  perfectly fine then there's no real need  for touch id anymore but the only  downside is that apple is requiring that  you either have an iphone 12 or newer  model since that's when they updated  face id to work at a wider angle which  potentially makes it more secure and  this is actually something that john  prosser leaked a long time ago so it's  awesome that we finally have this  feature in our hands but what i'm really  excited about is for when apple finally  gets rid of the notch with the upcoming  iphone 14 pro models which i recently  made a video on if you're interested in  that topic now getting back to ios 15.4  there are actually a few more cool  features that apple added to make it an  even better update if you're currently  paying for an icloud subscription you  can now finally create a custom email  domain for no extra charge at all this  is really awesome for small business  owners because the most popular way to  do this right now is with google  workspace which costs anywhere from six  to eighteen dollars a month so getting  it as a free bonus alongside an icloud  subscription is awesome and making it  even better you don't just get one  custom domain you get up to five custom  domains which is usually enough for a  small business going further icloud  keychain now allows you to add notes  under each password entry which can be  useful if you want to remind yourself  about something about a website or  anything else you want to write down  into the notes section and moving on a  really curious find from steve moser on  twitter is a new cosmetic scan trade-in  tool for the iphone so this will allow  you to do is to find out if your iphone  is actually eligible for trade-in if  you're unsure about any potential damage  being acceptable or not because in the  past you can send in an iphone for  trade-in only to discover that apple  didn't accept it due to cosmetic damage  or cracks but now you'll be able to use  your iphone's camera to scan the front  and the back of your iphone and if it  discovers major issues it'll let you  know that it is not eligible so both you  and apple don't have to waste time and  on top of that apple's trade-in partner  phobio has been getting a lot of  complaints about them secretly damaging  devices to lower trade-in values and  maybe this new feature will allow apple  to confirm that your device was in fact  in good condition when you shipped it  out for trade-in and another good point  is that since apple is now allowing  users to buy apple care up to 60 days  after their purchase they could use this  new cosmetic scan feature to make sure  that it's in good condition first which  will stop users from buying apple care  the second their display cracks to try  and get it covered under warranty now  going further apple has added a pretty  useful little widget for viewing your  apple card balance right from the widget  page so that it's harder to hide the  fact that you've been spending too much  money on apple products recently so yeah  thanks apple and now finally as a little  bonus that not everybody cares about  apple has added in a bunch of new emoji  with ios 15.4 which can come in handy  like the one where you're trying not to  look at your stock portfolio after this  crazy month but all in all i'd have to  say that ios 15.4 is probably the  biggest single update we've seen in a  long time which has single-handedly  fixed a lot of the complaints that  people had about the iphone 13 pro so  hopefully you learned something new from  this video and if you did go ahead and  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one and definitely  check out some of those videos right  over there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]

